From 5cda7f814b78b5c9861089495eb57d16abbdc9e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rams95 <rams95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:32:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0017-live-resolution-smaa-presets-key-art.patch

Inner resolution 1x-6x and 8x, changed while the game runs: the GPU memory is read back, the scale-sized buffers and the
programs (SCALE is a program constant) are made again and the memory goes back at the new scale (ps2::set_internal_scale).
The 2D art filter changes at once too (programs made again, decode cache reset). SMAA presets low / medium / high / ultra
(threshold and search lengths of the reference presets; ps2::set_smaa_quality; keys.ini smaa = off..ultra).
Key caps in the game's own style: the square symbol's thin rounded outline and the key's name in the game's letters, on a
2x font override when there is one.
Mouse look: open loop, one push per game step from the mouse movement of that step, no feedback (no overshoot);
modern direction by default, left/right and up/down invert switches, its own speed (keys.ini look_speed, 2.0).
Lens rain: drops and trails slant with the camera's turning (PS2_LENS_YAW); fast turns shake drops loose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
